sections.append(section('root-cause','Why the reference-model delay persists','<div class="callout">Shared resource: adapter replay scheduling and the go-back-N sequence domain.</div><figure class="timing-diagram"><img src="assets/replay-timing.svg" alt="Time-scaled trace from 2000 to 2110 ns. Client B transmits at 2012, is sequence-discarded at 2019 and 2031, reaches the receiver at 2043, commits at 2078, and completes at 2090 before Retrain at 2104."><figcaption>Absolute simulation time. Shaded interval spans sequence waiting and delivery; it is not a pure-wait measurement.</figcaption></figure><details><summary>Exact trace events and timestamps</summary><div class="timeline">'+''.join(f'<div><time>{t} ns</time><strong>{who}</strong><span>{what}</span></div>' for t,who,what in events)+'</div></details>'+p('Client B transmits while several flits are outstanding, then its request is discarded twice while the receiver awaits the expected sequence. Replay is scheduled ahead of new payload in the adapter. This supports coupling through the shared replay path; it does not support attributing B’s delay to a single occupied TX slot.')+p('The 2019–2043 ns interval spans observed sequence waiting and subsequent delivery, not a measured pure-wait counter. The trace does not decompose all 44 ns of added latency. Retrain at 2104 ns happens after B completes and cannot explain that completion delay.')+f'<p><a href="data/ref2x_cross_client_trace.csv">Full event CSV</a> · <a href="sources/ucie_adapter.cpp">Adapter scheduling code ↗</a></p>'))
